    {
      "id": "cb8-l2",
      "title": "Percent and Interest",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "Business math is mostly percentages. 19 % tax on a price is COMPUTE TAX ROUNDED = PRICE * 0.19. With ROUNDED, half a cent and more rounds up, like the tax office expects.",
        "Interest grows on itself: after 3 years at 5 %, the balance is BALANCE * 1.05 ** 3. COBOL works out the long decimals inside, and only rounds at the end.",
        "This exactness is why banks never moved away from COBOL: the result is the same on paper, at the bank and at the tax office."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
          "       PROGRAM-ID. INTEREST.",
          "       DATA DIVISION.",
          "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
          "       01 PRICE      PIC 9(4)V99 VALUE 49.99.",
          "       01 TAX        PIC 9(4)V99.",
          "       01 GROSS      PIC 9(4)V99.",
          "       01 SAVINGS    PIC 9(5)V99 VALUE 1000.",
          "       01 MONEY-OUT  PIC $$,$$9.99.",
          "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
          "           COMPUTE TAX ROUNDED = PRICE * 0.19.",
          "           COMPUTE GROSS = PRICE + TAX.",
          "           MOVE GROSS TO MONEY-OUT.",
          "           DISPLAY \"WITH TAX:      \" MONEY-OUT.",
          "           COMPUTE SAVINGS ROUNDED = SAVINGS * 1.05 ** 3.",
          "           MOVE SAVINGS TO MONEY-OUT.",
          "           DISPLAY \"AFTER 3 YEARS: \" MONEY-OUT.",
          "           STOP RUN."
        ],
        "output": [
          "WITH TAX:         $59.49",
          "AFTER 3 YEARS: $1,157.63"
        ]
      },
