    {
      "id": "cb8-l3",
      "title": "Exact All the Way",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "COMPUTE keeps many decimals while it works, and only cuts (or rounds) when the result goes into the field. So the order of the steps matters less than in other languages.",
        "Still, the field decides what's kept: 10 / 3 into a PIC 9V99 field is 3.33, and 3.33 * 3 is 9.99, not 10. Dividing last keeps more digits.",
        "So the rule from bank programmers: multiply first, divide last, round once."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
          "       PROGRAM-ID. ORDER.",
          "       DATA DIVISION.",
          "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
          "       01 THIRD   PIC 9V99.",
          "       01 RESULT  PIC 99V99.",
          "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
          "           COMPUTE THIRD = 10 / 3.",
          "           COMPUTE RESULT = THIRD * 3.",
          "           DISPLAY \"STEP BY STEP: \" RESULT.",
          "           COMPUTE RESULT = 10 * 3 / 3.",
          "           DISPLAY \"ONE FORMULA:  \" RESULT.",
          "           STOP RUN."
        ],
        "output": [
          "STEP BY STEP: 0999",
          "ONE FORMULA:  1000"
        ]
      },
